:18 (E), compare absolute Isa 66:9 (opposed to מוֺלִיד ); followed by infinitive 2Kin 4:24 ; with accusative of person alone 1Kin 18:44 hinder, stop ; with accusative of sky (hindering rain) Deut 11:17 ; 2Chr 7:13 ; passive participle absolute shut up , or hindered (for reasons not given) Jer 36:5 ; Neh 6:10 (? by a vow, or by ceremonial uncleanness, compare Rs Sem i. 436 f., 2nd ed. 455 f. ); = shut up (with ב , in prison) 2Kin 17:4 , passive participle Jer 33:1 ; 39:15 , figurative 20:9 ; on וְעָזוּב עָצוּר (5 t.) see I. עזב ; לָנוּ עֲצֻרָה 1Sam 21:6 women have been kept away with reference to us (compare RS l.c .); מִמְּנֵי עָצוּר 1Chr 12:1 kept away from before Saul; = detain , with accusative Judg 13:15-16 , in Job with ׳ע בְּמִלִּין בְּ, Job 4:2 , compare 29:9 , so בַּמַּיִם 12:5 ; ׳ע בְּעַמִּי 1Sam 9:17 is rule over , etc. (si vera lectio); insert also (with other words) 10:1 ᵐ5 We Dr and others 2 (late) retain , with accusative כֹּחַ 2Chr 13:20 ; 22:9 ; Dan 10:8 , 16 ; 11:6 ; + infinitive = be able to 1Chr 29:14 ; 2Chr 2:5 ; omit כֹּחַ 14:10 (+ עִמְּךָ ), 20:37 (+ infinitive). Niph`al be restrained, stayed , of plague: Perfect 3 feminine singular נֶעֱצָ֑רָה Numbers 17:15; Imperfect 3feminine singular תֵּעָצַר 2 Samuel 24:27 = 1Chr 21:22 , וַתֵּעָצַר Num 17:13 ; 25:8 (P) 2Sam 24:25 ; Psa 106:30 ; be shut up (of sky), Infinitive construct בְּהֵעָצֵר 1Kin 8:35 2Chr 6:26 ; be under restraint or detention Participle נֶעְצָר 1Sam 21:8 + י ׳לִפְחנֵי (? i.e. kept by a vow, compare HPS and Neh 6:10 above).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 1","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 1","1Chr 21 22","1Chr 29 14","1Kgs 8 35","1Kgs 14 10","1Kgs 18 44","1Kgs 21 21","1Sam 9 17"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":46,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 12 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עָצ֔וּר","source